  "body": "The maintainer asked for this research in chat on 2026-11-17:\n\n> Issue, needs-research; Router specific milling. Might need its own tabb, like milling, turning etc. But holds functions like Nesting, Grain matching, multiple spindle drill heads and so on.. This is what we need to research.. What is popular for example check cloudcuts capability that is specifically targeting routers.\n\nThis is a research issue. It gets no code, no branch and no PR. The research answers the questions in comments and files the sub-issues.\n\n**Questions**\n1. Which functions do the popular CAM products for CNC routers have that a milling CAM does not have? Make a list with one line for each function.\n2. What does CloudCuts offer for routers? Use only its public pages and public documents. Record behaviour only.\n3. Which other router products are popular? Examples to check: nesting-based sheet products for cabinet work and sign work. Name each source.\n4. Nesting: the research and the sub-issues are in #2156 and #2158 to #2166. What do those issues not cover for a router workflow?\n5. Grain matching: how does a user state the grain direction of a sheet and of a part? How does the nesting obey it? How does a product keep the grain continuous across adjacent parts?\n6. Multiple-spindle drill heads (drill blocks, gang drills): how does a machine file describe the spindles and their offsets? How does a post select one or more spindles for a hole pattern? Which controls and which G-code or M-code words are public?\n7. Other router functions to judge: tabs and onion skin, small-part hold-down order, vacuum zones, sheet labels, remnants, dogbone and T-bone corners, tool changes on an aggregate head.\n8. Does CamCraft need a Router tab beside Milling and Turning? Or does a machine type that shows and hides operations on the Milling tab do the work? Give one recommendation and the reason.\n\n**Rules for the research**\n- Clean-Room Protocol: use public documentation and published literature only. Do not copy text, UI strings, names or images of a product.\n- The machine research in #1907 and #1918 has router controller data. Link it, do not repeat it.\n- Each proposed function gets one sub-issue with `source:agent`, one priority, one effort label and its area labels.\n\nDone means:\n- Each question has an answer in a comment, with its public sources.\n- The sub-issues are filed and linked here.\n- The decision on the Router tab is put to the maintainer as one question.\n- Then this issue is closed.\n",
